{
  "name": "Refunds over the limit wait for a tap on WhatsApp",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nA refund request arrives on the webhook. Anything under the limit is refunded straight away. Anything over it stops here until a person taps **Approve** on WhatsApp, and only then does the money move.\n\nThe approval is the point: a refund cannot be taken back, and the person who can judge it is usually not at a desk.\n\n## Before you run it\n\n1. **Jabee credential** — API key from Management then Approvals at app.jabee.ai. Whoever will be asked verifies their phone on the Alerts page, under *Where alerts go*.\n2. **Header Auth credential** for Stripe — `Authorization` / `Bearer sk_live_...`. Or replace both HTTP Request nodes with whatever your irreversible step actually is.\n3. **Set the limit** in *Needs a person?* — it is 50000, which is 500.00 in Stripe's minor units.\n\n## The two things worth copying\n\n**External ID.** It is set to `refund-<payment intent>`, so a rerun of this workflow, or a retry on the error branch, returns the request already made instead of asking somebody twice about the same refund.\n\n**Report Outcome.** Jabee knows the tap; only this workflow knows whether the refund actually went through. Reporting it back is what makes the history true a month later.\n\n## If the answer may take hours\n\n*Wait for the Answer* holds the execution open while it polls, capped here at 15 minutes. For a decision that can sit overnight, drop it to off and act on the answer in a second workflow started by the **Jabee Trigger** node — see `approval-answered-trigger.json` beside this file.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Read me first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-520, -60]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "refund-requested",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Refund requested",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [-40, 180],
      "webhookId": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "amount-over-limit",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.amount }}",
              "rightValue": 50000,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Needs a person?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [200, 180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "approval",
        "operation": "request",
        "title": "=Refund {{ ($json.body.amount / 100).toFixed(2) }} {{ $json.body.currency.toUpperCase() }} to {{ $json.body.customer_email }}",
        "body": "={{ \"Reason given: \" + $json.body.reason + \"\\n\" + \"Payment: \" + $json.body.payment_intent + \"\\n\\n\" + \"Approve and the refund goes out now. Skip and nothing happens.\" }}",
        "options": ["approve", "skip"],
        "wait": true,
        "waitTimeout": 900,
        "additionalFields": {
          "external_id": "=refund-{{ $json.body.payment_intent }}",
          "url": "=https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments/{{ $json.body.payment_intent }}",
          "expires_in_minutes": 1440,
          "metadata": "={{ JSON.stringify({ payment_intent: $json.body.payment_intent, n8n_execution: $execution.id }) }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Ask before refunding",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-jabee.jabee",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [440, 80]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "status-approved",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
              "rightValue": "approved",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Approved?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [680, 80]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.stripe.com/v1/refunds",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "form-urlencoded",
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "payment_intent",
              "value": "={{ $('Refund requested').item.json.body.payment_intent }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "amount",
              "value": "={{ $('Refund requested').item.json.body.amount }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Issue the refund",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [920, -20]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "approval",
        "operation": "reportOutcome",
        "approvalId": "={{ $('Ask before refunding').item.json.id }}",
        "outcome": "refunded",
        "note": "=Stripe refund {{ $json.id }}"
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Record that it went out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-jabee.jabee",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1160, -20]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "approval",
        "operation": "reportOutcome",
        "approvalId": "={{ $json.id }}",
        "outcome": "not_refunded",
        "note": "=Answered {{ $json.status }}{{ $json.response_text ? ': ' + $json.response_text : '' }}"
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Record that it did not",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-jabee.jabee",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [920, 180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.stripe.com/v1/refunds",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "form-urlencoded",
        "bodyParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "payment_intent",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.payment_intent }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "amount",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.amount }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Refund without asking",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [440, 380]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Why two refund nodes\n\nThe small ones never reach a phone. Asking about every refund is how people learn to tap Approve without reading, which is worse than not asking at all.\n\n500 a month are included in the plan, so the limit is also what keeps the bill where you put it.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 340
      },
      "id": "0a1b2c3d-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a",
      "name": "Why two refund nodes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [800, 400]
    }
  ],
